{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TowerGeometricSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TowerGeometricSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Module.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uniform_bound_not_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uniform_bound_not_const","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L236-L248","doc":"The gap between the two results above, as a statement rather than a comment:\na uniform bound does NOT give level-independence.  Witnessed by an alternating\nresidual, which is uniformly bounded by `1` and not constant.\n\n(Still true and still the right statement — but note the ACTUAL residual is not\nmerely non-constant, it is `lam ^ n`; see `towerSum_iterated`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerFactor_le_simple_of_uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerFactor_le_simple_of_uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L227-L234","doc":"**No admissible `L_q` raises the tower factor above `1/(1 − ℏ_q²)`.**  If the\nleading-mode residual `Δ^{(n)} = λⁿ` is uniformly bounded in `n` (the content of\n`prop:delta-max-uniform-bound`) then the tower factor is at most the implemented\none, whatever `L_q` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerFactor_le_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerFactor_le_simple","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L215-L225","doc":"**The tower-factor ceiling.**  For `0 ≤ λ ≤ 1` the iterated tower factor\n`1/(1 − ℏ_q² λ)` is at most the implemented `1/(1 − ℏ_q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.lam_le_one_of_pow_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.lam_le_one_of_pow_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L202-L213","doc":"**A uniformly bounded power sequence has ratio at most `1`.**  If\n`|λⁿ| ≤ M` for every `n` then `λ ≤ 1`: for `λ > 1` the powers are unbounded\n(Archimedean property).  With `Δ^{(n)} = λ₁ⁿ` and `M = Δ_max` this is the\nstatement that `prop:delta-max-uniform-bound` forces `λ₁ ≤ 1`, i.e.\n`L_q ≥ √ℏ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.leadingMode_lam_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.leadingMode_lam_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L194-L200","doc":"At the leading mode `[1]_q = 1`, so `λ_1 = ℏ_q / L_q²`, and `λ_1 = 1` pins\n`L_q² = ℏ_q`.  Stated on `L_q²` so no square root is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated_eq_simple_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated_eq_simple_iff","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L181-L192","doc":"**The implemented factor `1/(1 - ℏ_q²)` is the `lam = 1` member of that\nfamily, and only that one.**  So adopting it is adopting `λ_k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L164-L179","doc":"**The tower of an ITERATED residual.**  With `Δ^{(n)}` the `n`-th iterate,\neigenvalue `lam ^ n`, the tower is geometric in `ℏ_q² · lam`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_le_of_uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_le_of_uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L91-L109","doc":"**What the corpus actually proves buys you: a bound, not the value.**\nGiven only `|Δ^{(n)}| ≤ M` uniformly in `n` — which is exactly\n`delta_max_uniform_bound` — the geometric expression bounds the tower's\nmagnitude termwise.\n\nStated termwise rather than on the `tsum` so it carries no summability\nhypothesis: each partial sum is dominated, which is the honest content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_of_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_of_const","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L67-L89","doc":"**The identity `tower_summed` uses.**  A tower `Σ_n ℏ_q^{2n} · Δ` whose\nresidual is LEVEL-INDEPENDENT sums to `Δ / (1 - ℏ_q²)`.\n\nThis is where the `1/(1 - ℏ_q²)` in `qbeta_e0.tower_summed` comes from: the\n`ℏ_q^{2n}` is the brane tower's structural grading, and `Δ^{(n)} = Δ` is the\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_sq_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_sq_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L51-L65","doc":"At `q > 1` the tower ratio `ℏ_q²` is in `[0, 1)`, so the grading converges.\nAt the substrate pin `q₀ ≈ 1.11` this gives `ℏ_q² ≈ 0.0098`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L48-L49","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 - 1/q`, the substrate deformation parameter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}